# Cursor Rules for GOrbit Project

## Test Execution
- When running tests via npm test or vitest, always use the `--run` flag to prevent watch mode
- Tests should execute once and exit, not wait for file changes
- Example: `npm test -- --run radar.test.ts` instead of `npm test -- radar.test.ts`

## General Guidelines
- Always use non-interactive flags for commands that might wait for user input
- Prefer one-shot execution over watch/daemon modes when running commands programmatically

